---
layout: layouts/enterprise.njk
navActive: industries
title: "Cybersecurity Solutions for Logistics Industry | CipherTrivia"
description: "Keep supply chains moving with logistics cybersecurity services by CipherTrivia, that uncovers vulnerabilities in fleet management software and warehouse systems or shipment tracking platforms."
crumbs: [["Home", "/"], ["Industries", "/industries/"], ["Logistics"]]
---
{% from "partials/enterprise/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{% from "partials/enterprise/icons.njk" import icon %}
{%- set faqs = [
  ["Why is cybersecurity important for logistics companies?", "Logistics companies depend on connected systems to coordinate shipments and manage fleets or process warehouse operations. Cybersecurity helps reduce the risk of ransomware and data breaches while supporting reliable deliveries and business continuity."],
  ["Can you test transportation management systems (TMS) and warehouse management systems (WMS)?", "Yes. Security assessments can identify vulnerabilities in TMS and WMS platforms involving authentication and access controls or insecure integrations and exposure of sensitive shipment or inventory data."],
  ["Do you provide cybersecurity testing for fleet management and GPS tracking systems?", "Yes. Assessments can examine fleet management applications and connected tracking systems for weak authentication and insecure communications or exposed interfaces that could compromise vehicle data and operational visibility."],
  ["How much do logistics cybersecurity services cost?", "Pricing depends on the number of applications and infrastructure assets in scope along with system complexity and testing depth. CipherTrivia can provide a quotation after reviewing your security requirements and assessment objectives."],
  ["Will cybersecurity testing disrupt logistics operations?", "Testing is planned around operational requirements and system sensitivity. Critical fleet platforms and warehouse systems may require controlled testing windows and agreed safeguards to minimize disruption."],
  ["How long does a logistics cybersecurity assessment take?", "The timeline depends on the number of systems being tested and the complexity of the logistics environment. A focused application assessment may take several days while larger environments with multiple warehouses and integrations may require several weeks."],
  ["Can you assess third-party integrations and logistics APIs?", "Yes. We assess APIs connecting logistics platforms with carriers and suppliers or payment systems to identify authorization weaknesses and excessive data exposure or insecure integrations."],
  ["Do your logistics cybersecurity services cover cloud infrastructure?", "Yes. Cloud security assessments examine hosted logistics applications and storage environments for misconfigurations and excessive permissions or exposed resources that could compromise shipment records and customer data."],
  ["Do you provide a report with remediation recommendations?", "Yes. CipherTrivia delivers a security assessment report detailing identified vulnerabilities and severity ratings alongside technical evidence and prioritized recommendations for remediation."],
  ["Can you retest vulnerabilities after fixes are implemented?", "Yes. We can retest reported vulnerabilities within the agreed scope to verify that remediation has addressed the identified issues and highlight any remaining security gaps."],
  ["Which compliance frameworks are relevant to logistics cybersecurity?", "Relevant frameworks may include ISO/IEC 27001 and the NIST Cybersecurity Framework alongside GDPR and PCI DSS when applicable. Requirements depend on the organization's operations and the types of data it processes."],
  ["How can we get started with CipherTrivia's logistics cybersecurity services?", "Contact CipherTrivia with details about your fleet management systems and warehouse platforms alongside your security concerns and assessment goals. Our team can recommend an appropriate scope and provide a proposed timeline and quotation."]
] %}
{#- Challenges: icon + its node position on the attack-surface map (clockwise from top left;
    ten nodes sit three along the top and bottom, two down each side) -#}
{%- set challenges = [
  ["shield-crack", "12%", "12%", 48, 48, "Ransomware and Supply Chain Disruptions", "Ransomware can block access to logistics systems and disrupt dispatch operations or delay shipments."],
  ["truck", "50%", "12%", 200, 48, "Fleet Management and GPS Security Risks", "Vulnerabilities in fleet management and GPS tracking systems can expose vehicle locations and increase cargo security risks."],
  ["database", "88%", "12%", 352, 48, "Shipment Data Breaches", "Weak access controls and insecure databases can expose delivery addresses and customer records or confidential shipping documents."],
  ["api", "88%", "37.25%", 352, 149, "Insecure APIs and System Integrations", "Vulnerable APIs connecting logistics platforms can expose shipment records or allow unauthorized changes to operational data."],
  ["wifi", "88%", "62.75%", 352, 251, "Warehouse Automation and IoT Vulnerabilities", "Insecure connected sensors and automated warehouse equipment can expose industrial systems to unauthorized access and operational disruption."],
  ["dependency", "88%", "88%", 352, 352, "Third-Party and Vendor Security Risks", "Compromised vendor accounts and insecure partner integrations can provide attackers with access to logistics networks."],
  ["key", "50%", "88%", 200, 352, "Unauthorized Remote Access", "Weak authentication and excessive permissions in remote access systems can expose critical logistics applications and infrastructure."],
  ["cloud-alert", "12%", "88%", 48, 352, "Cloud Security Misconfigurations", "Incorrect cloud permissions and exposed storage can leave shipment records and customer information accessible to unauthorized users."],
  ["mail-alert", "12%", "62.75%", 48, 251, "Phishing and Business Email Compromise", "Fraudulent emails can steal employee credentials or manipulate payment instructions and shipment requests."],
  ["eye-off", "12%", "37.25%", 48, 149, "Limited Visibility Across Distributed Operations", "Fragmented monitoring across warehouses and transport hubs can delay threat detection and incident response."]
] %}
{#- Services: icon, matching service page (empty when there is no dedicated page), title, text -#}
{%- set services = [
  ["target", "/services/penetration-testing/", "Penetration Testing for Logistics Systems", "We simulate realistic cyberattacks against logistics applications and supporting infrastructure to uncover exploitable vulnerabilities before attackers can use them to compromise business operations."],
  ["magnifier", "/services/vapt-security-services/", "Vulnerability Assessment", "We identify outdated software and insecure configurations or known vulnerabilities across logistics networks and applications, helping teams prioritize remediation based on risk."],
  ["browser", "/services/web-application-security-testing/", "Web Application and API Security Testing", "We assess shipment tracking portals and transportation management systems (TMS) alongside warehouse management systems (WMS) and APIs to uncover access control flaws and data exposure risks."],
  ["network", "/services/network-security-testing/", "Network Security Assessment", "We examine logistics networks and connected infrastructure to identify exposed services and weak segmentation or unauthorized access paths that could compromise operational systems."],
  ["cloud-lock", "/services/cloud-security-services/", "Cloud Security Assessment", "We review cloud-hosted logistics applications and storage environments for misconfigurations and excessive permissions or exposed resources that could put shipment and customer data at risk."],
  ["truck", "", "Fleet Management and IoT Security Testing", "We assess fleet management platforms and connected tracking devices for insecure communications and weak authentication or vulnerabilities that could expose vehicle data and logistics operations."],
  ["key", "", "Remote Access Security Assessment", "We evaluate remote maintenance connections and vendor access mechanisms to identify weak authentication and excessive permissions that could expose critical logistics systems."],
  ["doc-check", "/services/security-compliance/", "Security Compliance Assessment", "We assess relevant security controls against applicable standards and frameworks to identify gaps in data protection and access management or information security practices."],
  ["retest", "", "Retesting and Remediation Validation", "We retest identified vulnerabilities after fixes are implemented to verify remediation and highlight any remaining security weaknesses within the agreed scope."]
] %}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Service",
      "name": "Cybersecurity Solutions for the Logistics Industry",
      "serviceType": "Cybersecurity Services",
      "description": "Keep supply chains moving with logistics cybersecurity services by CipherTrivia, that uncovers vulnerabilities in fleet management software and warehouse systems or shipment tracking platforms.",
      "url": "https://www.ciphertrivia.com/industries/logistics/",
      "areaServed": "Worldwide",
      "audience": { "@type": "BusinessAudience", "audienceType": "Logistics and supply chain companies" },
      "provider": { "@id": "https://www.ciphertrivia.com/#organization" },
      "hasOfferCatalog": {
        "@type": "OfferCatalog",
        "name": "How CipherTrivia Helps Address These Challenges",
        "itemListElement": [
          {%- for s in services %}
          { "@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": { "@type": "Service", "name": {{ s[2] | dump | safe }} } }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
          {%- endfor %}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.ciphertrivia.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Industries", "item": "https://www.ciphertrivia.com/industries/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Logistics" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {%- for q in faqs %}
        { "@type": "Question", "name": {{ q[0] | dump | safe }}, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ q[1] | dump | safe }} } }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
</script>

